{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":41063,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"46a0ee18ef080704749c33297f624ab1b08520458982432f3889e34cb7be0efd","packTokens":26143,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":26063,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session and return the user's role.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active Buyer account buyer@a.test with a known password, linked to an active company when POST /auth/sign-in with that email and password then The response status is 200 and the response contains a session token and the role value \\\"Buyer\\\"\",\n    \"Given The session token returned in AC-1.1 when The user requests their own account details with that token then The response status is 200 and the returned email field is buyer@a.test\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject it with one identical invalid-credentials error message and return no session token.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active account buyer@a.test when POST /auth/sign-in with a wrong password then The response status is 401, the error message is \\\"Invalid email or password\\\" and no session token is returned\",\n    \"Given No account exists for ghost@x.test when POST /auth/sign-in with ghost@x.test and any password then The response status is 401 and the error message is identical to the one in AC-2.1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an account has 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account for 15 minutes from the fifth failure and reject every sign-in attempt during the lock with a temporary-lock error.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active account that has just had 4 consecutive failed sign-in attempts when A 5th sign-in with a wrong password is made then The response status is 423 and the error message says the account is temporarily locked\",\n    \"Given An account that has just had 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts when A sign-in with the correct password is made 1 minute later then The response status is 423 and the error message says the account is temporarily locked\",\n    \"Given An account locked at time T when The correct password is submitted at T + 15 minutes + 1 second (test clock) then The response status is 200 and a session token is returned\",\n    \"Given An account with 4 failed attempts followed by 1 successful sign-in when 4 more failed attempts are made then Each response status is 401 (not 423) and the account record lock field is empty\",\n    \"Given The account from AC-3.4 after its 4 further failed attempts when The correct password is submitted then The response status is 200, showing the failure count was reset by the earlier successful sign-in\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a user is deactivated or belongs to an inactive customer company, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in attempts and every request, including order submission, made with that user's existing sessions.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user deactivated by an administrator when The user signs in with the correct password then The response status is 403 and the error message says the account is inactive\",\n    \"Given An active Buyer whose customer company has been set inactive when The Buyer signs in with the correct password then The response status is 403 and no session token is returned\",\n    \"Given A Buyer holding a valid session token when An administrator deactivates the Buyer and the Buyer then requests the order list with the same token then The response status is 401\",\n    \"Given A Buyer holding a session token issued before an administrator deactivated them when POST /orders is called with that token and a valid basket then The response status is 401 and no order row is created\",\n    \"Given A Buyer of Fleet Co holding a session from before the company was set inactive when POST /orders is called then The response status is 401 or 403 and no order row is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session token.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user with a valid session token when The user calls POST /auth/sign-out and then requests GET /orders with the same token then The sign-out response status is a success status (200 or 204) and the GET /orders response status is 401\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any endpoint other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance carries no valid session token, then the portal shall reject it with status 401 without returning any record data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given No session token when GET the catalogue, the order list, an order, the invoice list and an invoice PDF then Each response status is 401 and no product, order or invoice data is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a user calls an endpoint outside the capabilities of their role (Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator, where Administrator includes every Office Staff capability), then the portal shall reject the request with status 403.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in Buyer when The Buyer requests the staff order queue then The response status is 403\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Office Staff user when The user POSTs a new price list then The response status is 403 and no price list record is created\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Office Staff user when POST /admin/products is called with a valid product then The response status is 403 and no product row is created\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator and an order in status Received when The Administrator requests the staff order queue and then confirms the order then Both response statuses are 200 and the order record status value is \\\"Confirmed\\\"\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a Buyer is signed in, the portal shall return only orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data that belong to the Buyer's own customer company, responding with status 404 to requests for such records of another company.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Buyer A of company A and order ORD-000200 of company B when Buyer A requests ORD-000200 then The response status is 404 and no order data is returned\",\n    \"Given Company B has invoice INV-000050 when Buyer A requests the PDF of INV-000050 then The response status is 404 and no file is returned\",\n    \"Given Company A has 3 orders (2 by Buyer A, 1 by colleague Buyer A2) and company B has 2 orders when Buyer A lists orders then The returned list contains exactly the 3 company A orders\",\n    \"Given Company B has a delivery address and a price list different from company A when Buyer A lists delivery addresses and opens a product then The returned address list contains only company A addresses and the returned price value comes from company A's price list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a password reset is requested for an email address, the portal shall return the same response whether or not the email exists and send a reset email with a single-use link valid for the configured period (default 1 hour) only if the email belongs to an active (including temporarily locked) account whose customer company, if any, is active.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active account exists for buyer@a.test when POST a password reset request for buyer@a.test then The response status is 202 and exactly one email containing a reset link is sent to buyer@a.test\",\n    \"Given No account exists for ghost@x.test when POST a password reset request for ghost@x.test then The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1 and no email is sent\",\n    \"Given A user deactivated by an administrator when POST a password reset request for that user's email then The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1 and no email is sent\",\n    \"Given A pending invitee who has not yet accepted the invitation when POST a password reset request for that invitee's email then The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1, no email is sent and the user record status stays \\\"Pending\\\"\",\n    \"Given An active Buyer whose customer company has been set inactive when POST a password reset request for that Buyer's email then The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1 and no email is sent\",\n    \"Given An active account temporarily locked after 5 failed sign-in attempts when POST a password reset request for that account's email then The response status is 202 and exactly one reset email is sent to that address\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user submits a new password through an unexpired, unused reset link, the portal shall replace the password, invalidate the link and clear any sign-in lock on the account.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A reset link issued 10 minutes ago when The user submits a new password through it and then signs in with the new and the old password then The reset response status is 200, the new-password sign-in response status is 200 and the old-password response status is 401\",\n    \"Given An account locked after 5 failed attempts and a valid reset link for it when The user completes a password reset and signs in with the new password within the 15-minute lock period then The sign-in response status is 200\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a reset link is expired or already used, or its user is pending, deactivated or belongs to an inactive customer company when the link is used, then the portal shall reject the password change, keeping the existing password and any sign-in lock unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A reset link that has already been used when A new password is submitted through it again then The response status is 400 and the error message says the link is invalid or expired\",\n    \"Given A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with the default validity when A new password is submitted through it and then sign-in with the old password is attempted then The reset response status is 400 with an error saying the link is invalid or expired, and the old-password sign-in response status is 200\",\n    \"Given A reset link issued 5 minutes ago to an active Buyer, after which an administrator deactivated that Buyer when A new password is submitted through the link then The response status is 400 and the user record status value stays \\\"Deactivated\\\"\",\n    \"Given A reset link issued 5 minutes ago to a Buyer whose company was then set inactive when A new password is submitted through the link and the company is later reactivated and the Buyer signs in with the old password then The reset response status is 400 and the later old-password sign-in response status is 200\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator invites a user with name, email and the role Buyer (linked to a customer company) or Office Staff, the portal shall create a pending account and send an invitation email with a link valid for the configured period (default 7 days).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator and active company A when POST an invitation for new.buyer@a.test as Buyer of company A then The response status is 201, the user record has status \\\"Pending\\\" and one invitation email is sent to new.buyer@a.test\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator when POST an invitation with role \\\"Customer Account Manager\\\" then The response status is 400 and no user record is created\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator when POST an invitation for a Buyer without a customer company then The response is a validation error status (400/422) and the error names the company field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator invites a user with the role Administrator, the portal shall create a pending account and send an invitation email.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator when POST an invitation for new.admin@dist.test with role Administrator then The response status is 201, the user record has status \\\"Pending\\\" and role \\\"Administrator\\\", and one invitation email is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an invited user sets a password through an unexpired invitation link, the portal shall activate the account.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An invitation sent 2 days ago when The invitee sets a password through the link and signs in then The user record status is \\\"Active\\\" and the sign-in response status is 200\",\n    \"Given An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago with the default validity when The invitee tries to set a password through the link then The response status is 400 and the user record status stays \\\"Pending\\\"\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator resends the invitation of a pending account, the portal shall invalidate every previous invitation link for that user and send a new invitation email.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A pending account with an unused invitation link L1 when The administrator resends the invitation and the invitee then uses L1 then A new invitation email is sent and the response to using L1 has status 400\",\n    \"Given An expired pending invitation when The administrator resends it and the invitee accepts using the new link then A new invitation email is sent and the accept response status is 200\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let administrators list users with role, customer company and account status, associate a Buyer with a customer company, deactivate a user and reactivate a deactivated user, without deleting any of the user's orders or invoices.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Users of several roles and statuses (Pending, Active, Deactivated) when An administrator lists users then Each returned row contains the role, company and status fields\",\n    \"Given Buyer B has placed 3 orders when An administrator deactivates B and a staff user lists orders filtered by B's company then B's user record status is \\\"Deactivated\\\" and the returned list still contains B's 3 orders with placedBy B\",\n    \"Given A deactivated Buyer of an active company when An administrator reactivates the user and the user signs in then The user record status is \\\"Active\\\" and the sign-in response status is 200\",\n    \"Given An Active Buyer of Acme Garage when An Administrator changes the user's company to Fleet Co and the user then calls GET /orders then The returned list contains only Fleet Co orders\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let administrators change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Buyer user when An administrator changes the role to Office Staff and the user requests the staff order queue then The response status is 200\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let administrators change a user's role to Administrator.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Office Staff user Sam when An Administrator changes Sam's role to Administrator and Sam calls POST /admin/categories then The response status is 201\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an administrator tries to reactivate a deactivated user whose customer company is inactive, then the portal shall reject the reactivation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A deactivated Buyer of inactive company Fleet Co when POST /admin/users/{id}/reactivate is called then The response status is 409 with error code COMPANY_INACTIVE\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or brand contains the term, ignoring letter case.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Active products \\\"Brake Pad Set\\\" (code BP-100, part number 0986494, brand Bosch) and \\\"Oil Filter\\\" (code OF-20, brand Mann) when A Buyer searches \\\"brak\\\" then The returned list contains Brake Pad Set and does not contain Oil Filter\",\n    \"Given The products of AC-20.1 when A Buyer searches \\\"86494\\\", then \\\"bp-1\\\", then \\\"BOSCH\\\" then Each returned list contains Brake Pad Set\",\n    \"Given A retired product \\\"Brake Drum\\\" when A Buyer searches \\\"brake\\\" then The returned list does not contain Brake Drum\",\n    \"Given The products of AC-20.1 when A Buyer searches \\\"zzzz\\\" then The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer filters the catalogue by a category, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category that also match any supplied search term, returning all active products again once the category filter is cleared.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 3 active products in Filters and 2 in Brake system when A Buyer lists the catalogue filtered by Filters then The returned list count is 3 and every returned product has the category value Filters\",\n    \"Given The products of AC-21.1 when A Buyer lists the catalogue with no category filter then The returned list count is 5\",\n    \"Given Active products \\\"Oil Filter\\\" (Filters) and \\\"Oil Pump\\\" (Engine parts) when A Buyer searches \\\"oil\\\" filtered by Filters then The returned list contains Oil Filter only\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return only active products with a compatibility entry that matches every supplied value.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product P has a compatibility entry Ford, Focus, years 2015–2018, 1.0 EcoBoost, petrol when A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2017 then The returned list contains P\",\n    \"Given The same product P when A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2010 then The returned list does not contain P\",\n    \"Given P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost Petrol and P2 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 2.0 TDCi Diesel when A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2018, fuel Diesel then The returned list contains P2 only\",\n    \"Given Product A compatible with Ford Focus 2018 and product B compatible with Ford Fiesta 2018 when A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2018 then The returned list contains product A and not product B\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer lists the catalogue, the portal shall return only active products, each with image URL, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the Buyer's price and stock status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active product with all fields populated and a price on the Buyer's price list when A Buyer lists the catalogue then The returned row for that product contains imageUrl, name, productCode, manufacturer, unit, packSize, price and stockStatus fields with the stored values\",\n    \"Given Active product 'Brake Pad Set' and retired product 'Old Filter' when A Buyer lists the catalogue then The returned list contains 'Brake Pad Set' and does not contain 'Old Filter'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer opens an active product, the portal shall return its image, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price, stock status and compatible vehicles.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active product with 2 compatibility entries when A Buyer opens the product then The response status is 200 and the returned compatibility list has 2 entries alongside the other listed fields\",\n    \"Given An active product with imported quantity 0 when A Buyer opens the product then The response status is 200 and the stockStatus value is \\\"Out of stock\\\"\",\n    \"Given A retired product when A Buyer opens the product then The response status is 404\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall price every product shown to a Buyer, and every line of that company's basket, staff-created orders and repeat orders, from the price list assigned to the Buyer's customer company at the time of the request, so that a changed assignment applies from then on.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product X costs 50.00 on Standard and 40.00 on Workshop A, and company A is assigned Workshop A when A Buyer of company A opens product X then The returned price value is 40.00 and the value 50.00 does not appear in the response\",\n    \"Given The setup of AC-25.1 when An administrator assigns Standard to company A and the Buyer opens product X again then The returned price value is 50.00\",\n    \"Given Product BP-1001 priced 15.00 on Standard and 12.50 on Workshop A; company A on Workshop A and company B on Standard when A Buyer of each company opens BP-1001 then The price value returned to company A's Buyer is 12.50 and to company B's Buyer is 15.00\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff view the unit price a given customer company pays for a product, taken from that company's assigned price list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A is assigned Workshop A with BP-1001 = 12.50 and a signed-in Office Staff user when The user requests the price of BP-1001 for company A then The response status is 200 and the returned price value is 12.50\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a product has no price on the customer company's assigned price list, then the portal shall show the product as \\\"Price on request\\\" and reject adding it to a basket or order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Active product Y with no price on company A's price list when A Buyer of company A opens product Y then The returned price field is null and the price label value is \\\"Price on request\\\"\",\n    \"Given The same product Y when The Buyer adds product Y with quantity 1 to the basket then The response is a rejection status (422/400), the error says the product has no price and the basket line count is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let administrators create, rename and deactivate price lists, set, edit and remove at most one price per product on a price list, and assign an active price list to a customer company.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in Administrator when The administrator creates price list \\\"Fleet\\\", sets product X to 30.00 and then sets product X to 32.00 then The Fleet price list has 1 row for product X with value 32.00\",\n    \"Given Price list Fleet already has a price for product X when POST /admin/price-lists/{Fleet}/prices is called again for X then The response status is 409 with error code DUPLICATE_PRICE\",\n    \"Given Price list Fleet containing product X and assigned to company F when The administrator removes product X from Fleet and a Buyer of company F opens X then The price list row count for product X is 0 and the returned price label value is \\\"Price on request\\\"\",\n    \"Given A deactivated price list when The administrator assigns it to a customer company then The response status is 422 and the company's assigned price list value is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a price on a price list is changed or a company's price list assignment changes, the portal shall leave the unit prices stored on existing orders and invoices unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Order ORD-000101 has a line for product X at unit price 40.00 when The administrator changes product X to 45.00 on that price list and the order is opened then The returned unit price value on the order line is 40.00\",\n    \"Given Order ORD-000124 with BP-1001 at 12.50 for company A when An administrator reassigns company A to Standard and the Buyer opens ORD-000124 then The returned line unit price is 12.50 and the order total value is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall derive each product's stock status as Out of stock when its imported quantity is 0 or less or it has never been imported, Low stock when the quantity is from 1 up to the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock when the quantity is above that threshold.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Low-stock threshold 5 when The stock-status calculator is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6 then The returned values are Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock\",\n    \"Given Low-stock threshold 5 when The stock-status calculator is called for a product with no imported quantity then The returned value is Out of stock\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the scheduled stock import finds a new ERP CSV file in the configured location that passes file validation, the portal shall replace the stored quantity and recalculate the stock status of each listed known product and record a successful import log entry with row counts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Threshold 10, products BP-1001 (quantity 4) and FL-200 (quantity 0) and a valid CSV listing BP-1001=25 and FL-200=3 when The stock import job runs then The BP-1001 row has quantity 25 and status \\\"In stock\\\", the FL-200 row has quantity 3 and status \\\"Low stock\\\", and an import log record has status \\\"Success\\\" with rows-applied count 2\",\n    \"Given No new file in the configured location since the last run when The stock import job runs then No stock quantity value changes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a valid ERP CSV contains rows with unknown product identifiers, then the portal shall skip those rows, apply the other rows and list the unknown identifiers in the import log entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid CSV with BP-100=12 and ZZ-999=5, where ZZ-999 is not a known product when The stock import job runs then BP-100's stored quantity value is 12 and the import log row has status \\\"Success\\\", rows-applied count 1 and ZZ-999 in its skipped-identifiers list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the ERP CSV file is missing, unreadable, empty, lacks a required column or contains a non-numeric or negative quantity, then the portal shall keep every previous stock quantity unchanged and record a failed import log entry with the failure reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Stored quantity BP-100=12 and a CSV missing the quantity column when The stock import job runs then BP-100's stored quantity value is still 12 and an import log row has status \\\"Failed\\\" and a reason naming the missing column\",\n    \"Given Stored quantity BP-100=12 and a CSV where one row has quantity \\\"abc\\\" and another has BP-100=20 when The stock import job runs then BP-100's stored quantity value is still 12 and the import log row has status \\\"Failed\\\" with a reason naming the bad row\",\n    \"Given An empty CSV file when The stock import job runs then No stored quantity value changes and the import log row has status \\\"Failed\\\"\",\n    \"Given No CSV file is present at the configured location when The stock import job runs then An import log record has status \\\"Failed\\\" with reason \\\"file missing\\\" and no stock row changes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user or administrator lists stock imports, the portal shall return each import's time, status, rows-applied count, skipped identifiers and failure reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given One successful and one failed import when A staff user lists stock imports then The response status is 200 and the returned list has 2 rows with time, status, rowsApplied, skippedIdentifiers and failureReason fields\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Buyer when The Buyer lists stock imports then The response status is 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall not send any create, update or delete request to the ERP system.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Outbound traffic to the ERP host is recorded and the ERP CSV file checksum is noted when The stock import job runs and a Buyer submits an order then No outbound call to the ERP host is recorded and the CSV file checksum value is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user opens a product, the portal shall return its imported stock quantity, stock status, the time of the last successful import and its price on each price list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product X with quantity 7 and prices on Standard and Workshop A when A staff user opens product X then The returned quantity value is 7 and the returned price list has 2 entries\",\n    \"Given Product P imported with quantity 30 at 02:00 when A staff user requests the stock of P then The response contains quantity 30, status \\\"In stock\\\" and last import time 02:00\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a Buyer basket line or staff-created order line would have a quantity greater than the product's imported stock quantity or the product is Out of stock, or a staff amendment would raise a line's quantity above the product's imported stock quantity, then the portal shall reject the change with an error stating the available quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product BP-100 with imported quantity 10 when A Buyer sets the basket quantity to 11 then The response is a rejection status (422/400), the error message states 10 available and the line quantity value stays at its previous value\",\n    \"Given The same product when A Buyer sets the basket quantity to 10 then The response status is 200 and the returned line quantity is 10\",\n    \"Given Product FL-200 with imported quantity 0 when A Buyer adds FL-200 quantity 1 to the basket then The response is a rejection status and the basket list does not contain FL-200\",\n    \"Given Product OF-20 with imported quantity 0 when A staff user adds 1 of OF-20 to an order being created for company A then The response status is 422 and the error message says the product is out of stock\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 5 of OF-20, and a stock import has since set OF-20 to quantity 0 when Staff change the OF-20 line quantity to 2 then The response status is 200 and the returned OF-20 line quantity value is 2\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 2 lines, one of which is OF-20 with imported quantity 0 when Staff remove the OF-20 line then The response status is 200 and the order record has 1 line, without OF-20\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 2 of BP-100 and BP-100 imported quantity 3 when Staff change the BP-100 line quantity to 4 then The response is a rejection status (422/400), the error message states 3 available and the line quantity value stays 2\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall keep each Buyer's basket for the duration of the Buyer's session only, letting the Buyer add products, change line quantities (minimum 1) and remove lines, and returning each line's unit price, quantity and line total and the tax-exclusive basket subtotal.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product X at 12.50 and product Z at 4.00 on the Buyer's price list, both in stock when The Buyer adds 2 of X and 3 of Z then The returned line totals are 25.00 and 12.00 and the subtotal value is 37.00\",\n    \"Given The basket from AC-38.1 when The Buyer changes X to quantity 3 and removes the Z line then The returned line count is 1, the line total is 37.50 and the subtotal value is 37.50\",\n    \"Given The basket from AC-38.1 when The Buyer sets X to quantity 0 or -1 then The response status is 422, the error names the quantity field and the line quantity value stays 2\",\n    \"Given A Buyer with 2 basket lines when The Buyer lists the catalogue and then requests the basket in the same session then The returned basket has the same 2 lines\",\n    \"Given A Buyer with 2 basket lines when The Buyer signs out, signs in again and requests the basket then The returned basket line count is 0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date, in the configured timezone, as the next working day when the order time is before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and as the working day after the next working day when the order time is at or after the cutoff, skipping configured non-working dates.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Cutoff 14:00, Saturday and Sunday non-working, Monday 5 Oct 2026 a working day when The delivery-date calculator is called with Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00 then The returned values are Tuesday 6 Oct, Wednesday 7 Oct and Wednesday 7 Oct\",\n    \"Given Cutoff 14:00, weekends non-working when The calculator is called with Friday 13:00 and Friday 15:00 then The returned values are the following Monday and the following Tuesday\",\n    \"Given Cutoff 14:00 and Tuesday 6 Oct 2026 listed as a non-working date when The calculator is called with Monday 5 Oct 13:00 then The returned value is Wednesday 7 Oct\",\n    \"Given Timezone Europe/London and cutoff 14:00 when The calculator is called with Monday 12:30 UTC during British Summer Time (13:30 local) then The returned value is Tuesday\",\n    \"Given Timezone Europe/London and cutoff 14:00 when The calculator is called with Monday 5 Oct 2026 13:30 UTC (14:30 local) then The returned value is Wednesday 7 Oct\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall accept as a delivery date for Buyer baskets, submitted orders and staff-created orders only a working day from the earliest delivery date up to the configured maximum number of days ahead, checked at submission time, offering exactly those dates as selectable and rejecting any other date with an error naming the delivery date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Maximum 14 days ahead, weekends non-working, current time Monday 10:00 when A Buyer requests the selectable delivery dates then The returned list starts with Tuesday, contains no Saturday or Sunday, and its last value is no later than 14 days after today\",\n    \"Given Now is Monday 2026-10-05 15:00, cutoff 14:00, maximum 30 days ahead when The Buyer sets the basket delivery date to 2026-10-06, 2026-10-10 (Saturday) and 2026-11-20 in turn then Each response is a validation error status with an error naming the date rule broken\",\n    \"Given The settings of AC-40.2 when The Buyer sets the basket delivery date to 2026-10-07 then The response status is 200 and the basket delivery date field is 2026-10-07\",\n    \"Given A Buyer basket with delivery date Tuesday chosen at Monday 13:50 when The Buyer submits the order at Monday 14:05 then The response status is 422, the error names the deliveryDate field and no order record is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a basket, submitted order or order edit is given a delivery address that does not belong to the order's customer company, then the portal shall reject it with an error naming the delivery address.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Buyer of company A when The Buyer submits an order using a delivery address id of company B then The response status is 422, the error names the deliveryAddress field and no order record is created\",\n    \"Given Company A has addresses A1 and A2 and company B has address B1 when A Buyer of company A sets the basket delivery address to B1 then The response status is 422 and the basket delivery address field is unchanged\",\n    \"Given The data of AC-41.2 when A Buyer of company A sets the basket delivery address to A2 then The response status is 200 and the basket delivery address field is A2\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer submits an order, the portal shall re-check every line's availability, stock limit and current company price and, if any line is unavailable, over stock or re-priced, reject the submission and list the affected lines with their current price and available quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A basket with 5 of BP-100 when 12 were in stock, and a stock import then sets BP-100 to 3 when The Buyer submits the order then The response status is 409, the returned list of affected lines contains BP-100 with available quantity 3, and no order record is created\",\n    \"Given A basket line for product X at 40.00, and the administrator then changes X to 42.00 when The Buyer submits the order then The response status is 409, the returned affected line shows current price 42.00 and no order record is created\",\n    \"Given A basket line whose product was retired after it was added when The Buyer submits the order then The response status is 409 and the response lists the line as unavailable\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer proceeds to checkout, the portal shall display a final review page with the lines, quantities, unit prices, line totals, subtotal, delivery address, delivery date and note before the submit action.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Buyer with a 2-line basket, a selected address, date and note when The Buyer proceeds to checkout in a browser then A person checks that the review page is shown with every listed item matching the basket, with the submit button below them, and that the order is only created after pressing submit\",\n    \"Given A basket with 2 lines, a chosen address, date and note 'Rear entrance' when GET /checkout/review is called then The response contains both lines with prices and totals, the subtotal, the address, the date and the note value 'Rear entrance'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a valid order is submitted, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential prefixed order number, its lines at order-time unit prices, a copy of the delivery address, the delivery date, the optional note, status Received and a first timeline entry, and then empty the basket.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Prefix ORD- and last order number ORD-000123 when A Buyer submits a valid basket with 2 lines and note \\\"Leave at rear gate\\\" then The response status is 201 and the returned order has number ORD-000124, status Received, 2 lines with the basket unit prices, the address, the date, the note value and 1 timeline entry naming the Buyer\",\n    \"Given The order from AC-44.1 when A staff user lists Received orders in the queue and the Buyer requests the basket then The queue list contains ORD-000124 and the returned basket line count is 0\",\n    \"Given A valid basket with no note when The Buyer submits the order then The response status is 201 and the order note field is empty\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a user of an inactive customer company or a deactivated user submits an order, or staff try to create an order for an inactive customer company, then the portal shall reject it with an error and create no order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A set inactive when A staff user submits a new order for company A with valid lines then The response is a rejection status (422/409), the error says the company is inactive and no order record is created\",\n    \"Given A Buyer whose session is still valid when the administrator deactivates them (race checked at submission) when The order submission is processed after deactivation then The response status is 401 or 403 and no order record is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order changes status, the portal shall append a timeline entry recording the new status, the date and time, and the user who made the change or 'System'.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order placed by Buyer Ann and confirmed by staff user Sam when The order is opened then The returned timeline list has 2 entries: 'Received' by Ann and 'Confirmed' by Sam, each with a timestamp\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall send each order email to the Buyer who placed the order while that Buyer is active and still linked to the order's customer company, and otherwise, including for orders created by staff, to the customer company's contact email.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order placed by active Buyer buyer@a.test of company A when Staff confirm the order then The confirmation email is sent to buyer@a.test only\",\n    \"Given An order created by staff for company A whose contact email is orders@a.test when Staff confirm the order then The confirmation email is sent to orders@a.test and not to any Buyer\",\n    \"Given A Received order placed by Buyer ann@a.test of company A (contact email orders@a.test), after which an administrator deactivated Ann when Staff confirm the order then The confirmation email is sent to orders@a.test and no email is sent to ann@a.test\",\n    \"Given A Picking order placed by Buyer ann@a.test of company A (contact email orders@a.test), after which an administrator moved Ann to Fleet Co when Staff set the order to Out for delivery then The out-for-delivery email is sent to orders@a.test and no email is sent to ann@a.test\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return every order of the Buyer's customer company, including orders placed by colleagues and by staff, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by status and order date range.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A has 1 order by Buyer A1, 1 by Buyer A2 and 1 created by staff when Buyer A1 lists orders then The returned list has 3 rows, each with orderNumber, orderDate, deliveryDate, deliveryAddress, total and status fields\",\n    \"Given Company A has one Delivered order by Buyer A2 and one Received order when Buyer A1 lists orders filtered by status Delivered then The returned list contains only the Delivered order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer of the order's company or a staff user opens an order, the portal shall return its number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, note and staff amendments.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order whose quantity of BP-1001 was amended by staff from 4 to 2 and which was then confirmed when A Buyer of that company opens the order then The response status is 200, the returned timeline has entries for Received and Confirmed with time and actor, and the amendments list has an entry showing BP-1001 changed from 4 to 2 with the staff user and time\",\n    \"Given An order containing a product that was later retired when A Buyer opens the order then The returned line still shows the product name, code and order-time unit price\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer cancels an order of their own company that is in Received status, the portal shall set its status to Cancelled and add a timeline entry with the Buyer and time.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order of company A placed by Buyer A2 when Buyer A1 cancels it then The response status is 200, the order status value is Cancelled and the last timeline entry names Buyer A1\",\n    \"Given A Received order created by staff for company A when Buyer A1 cancels it then The response status is 200 and the order status value is Cancelled\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a Buyer tries to cancel an order that is not in Received status, then the portal shall reject the request with an error telling the Buyer to contact the distributor office.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Confirmed order of the Buyer's company when The Buyer cancels it then The response status is 409, the error message tells the Buyer to contact the distributor office and the status value stays Confirmed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer repeats an order of their company, the portal shall add each still-orderable line to the session basket at the current price and the original quantity, capped at available stock and flagged when reduced, and flag lines that are retired, out of stock or without a price as unavailable, without creating an order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An old order with 4 of X (now 42.00, 10 in stock), 2 of R (now retired) and 6 of Z (now 3 in stock) when The Buyer repeats the order then The returned basket has X with quantity 4 at 42.00, Z with quantity 3 flagged as reduced, and R listed as unavailable and not added\",\n    \"Given A colleague's order with BP-1001 ×2 at 12.50 (now 13.00, stock 50) and FL-200 ×1 (now retired) when The Buyer repeats it then The response status is 200, the basket list contains BP-1001 quantity 2 at 13.00, the response flags FL-200 as unavailable, and the company's order count is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user lists orders, the portal shall return orders of all customers with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total and status, filtered by any supplied customer, order date range and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Orders for companies A and B in statuses Received and Picking when A staff user lists orders filtered by company A and status Received then Every returned row has customer A and status Received with the listed fields\",\n    \"Given Orders dated 1, 5 and 9 October when A staff user lists orders with order date range 4–6 October then The returned list contains only the 5 October order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user searches customers by partial company name or account number or opens a customer company, the portal shall return the matching customer companies or, for the opened company, its details, delivery addresses, assigned price list, users, active status, orders and invoices.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Companies \\\"Northside Motors\\\" (account C-1001) and \\\"Fleetline\\\" (C-2002) when A staff user searches \\\"north\\\" and then \\\"C-2002\\\" then The first returned list contains only Northside Motors and the second only Fleetline\",\n    \"Given Company Smith Motors with 2 addresses, 3 users, orders and invoices when A staff user opens the company then The response contains the company fields, an addresses list of count 2, the price list name, a users list of count 3, the status, and orders and invoices lists\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let staff edit an order only while it is in Received status, limited to changing line quantities, removing lines, changing the note, changing the delivery address to another address of the same company and changing the delivery date to a date selectable at the time of the edit.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order with delivery date Thursday when At Monday 15:00 staff change the date to Wednesday, then to Tuesday then The Wednesday change response status is 200 and the Tuesday change response status is 422 with an error naming the deliveryDate field\",\n    \"Given A Received order of company A when Staff change the delivery address to an address of company B then The response status is 422 and the order's address value is unchanged\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 2 lines when Staff remove one line and change the note then The response status is 200 and the order record has 1 line, the new note and a recalculated total\",\n    \"Given A Confirmed order when Staff change a line quantity then The response status is 409 and the line quantity value is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff change a line quantity or remove a line on a Received order, the portal shall record the amendment with old and new quantity, staff user and time, and send the order recipient an email listing each changed line with its old and new quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order with 5 of X when Staff change the quantity of X to 3 then An amendment record shows X 5 → 3 with the staff user and time, and one email naming X, 5 and 3 is sent to the order recipient\",\n    \"Given A Received order placed by Buyer Ann with BP-1001 ×4 and FL-200 ×1 when Staff set BP-1001 to 2 and remove FL-200 then An email is sent to Ann listing BP-1001 4→2 and FL-200 1→0\",\n    \"Given A Received order when Staff change only the delivery date, delivery address or note then No email is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff confirm an order in Received status whose lines are all active and within available stock and whose delivery address still exists, the portal shall set the status to Confirmed and add a timeline entry with the staff user and time, and otherwise reject the confirmation listing the failing lines.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order with all lines in stock when Staff confirm it then The response status is 200, the status value is Confirmed and the timeline entry records the staff user and time\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 5 of BP-100 while only 3 are in stock when Staff confirm it then The response status is 409, the error lists BP-100 with available quantity 3 and the status value stays Received\",\n    \"Given An order in status Picking when Staff confirm it then The response status is 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order becomes Confirmed, the portal shall send a confirmation email to the order recipient containing the order number, lines with quantities and unit prices, order total, delivery address, delivery date and every quantity change staff made before confirmation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Received order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer Ann where staff reduced BP-1001 from 4 to 2 when Staff confirm it then One email is sent to Ann containing ORD-000124, the lines, the total, the delivery date and address, and the change of BP-1001 from 4 to 2\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff advance an order's status, the portal shall accept only the next status in the sequence Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered (or a cancellation) and add a timeline entry with the staff user and time, rejecting any other change and leaving the status unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Confirmed order when Staff set it to Picking then The response status is 200 and the last timeline entry has status Picking, the staff user and the time\",\n    \"Given A Confirmed order when Staff set it to Out for delivery then The response status is 409 and the status value stays Confirmed\",\n    \"Given A Picking order when Staff set it back to Confirmed then The response status is 409\",\n    \"Given A Picking order when Staff set it to Out for delivery then The response status is 200 and the status value is Out for delivery\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall send the order recipient an email identifying the order number and stating it is out for delivery.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Picking order ORD-000124 when Staff set it to Out for delivery then One email containing ORD-000124 and the text \\\"out for delivery\\\" is sent to the order recipient\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff cancel or reject an order that is neither Delivered nor Cancelled, the portal shall require a reason, set the status to Cancelled, record the reason, staff user and time, and send the order recipient a cancellation email containing the reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Out for delivery order when Staff cancel it with reason \\\"Customer closed\\\" then The status value is Cancelled, the timeline entry records the reason, staff user and time, and an email containing \\\"Customer closed\\\" is sent\",\n    \"Given A Picking order placed by Buyer Ann when Staff cancel it with reason 'Supplier recall' then The response status is 200, the status value is Cancelled, the order row stores the reason, and an email containing 'Supplier recall' is sent to Ann\",\n    \"Given A Received order when Staff reject it with an empty reason then The response is a validation error status (400/422) and the status value stays Received\",\n    \"Given A Delivered order when Staff cancel it with a reason then The response status is 409 and the status value stays Delivered\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff submit an order on behalf of an active customer company with a company delivery address, products, quantities, a valid delivery date and optional note, the portal shall create it in Received status under the same price, stock, address and delivery-date rules as a Buyer order, marked as created by that staff user.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Active company A on price list Workshop A when A staff user submits an order for company A with 2 of X and a valid address and date then The response status is 201, the order has status Received, the line unit price comes from Workshop A and the createdBy field names the staff user\",\n    \"Given The order from AC-62.1 when A Buyer of company A lists orders then The returned list contains the order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall keep its existing orders and invoices visible to staff and let staff progress, cancel and invoice its open orders.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Picking order of a company that has been set inactive when Staff set it to Out for delivery then The response status is 200\",\n    \"Given An Out for delivery order of an inactive company when Staff set it to Delivered then The response status is 200 and one invoice record is created for that order\",\n    \"Given Inactive company Fleet Co with orders and invoices when Staff list orders and invoices filtered by Fleet Co then Both response statuses are 200 and the returned lists include Fleet Co's orders and invoices\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV file with one row per non-Cancelled order whose requested delivery date is that date, containing order number, customer name, delivery address, address contact name and phone, delivery date, line summary, order note and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given For 8 Oct: one Confirmed order, one Out for delivery order and one Cancelled order; for 9 Oct: 1 order when Staff export the delivery list for 8 Oct then The returned file is CSV (content type text/csv) with a header row and exactly 2 data rows, for the Confirmed and Out for delivery orders, each with the listed columns\",\n    \"Given An order for today when Staff export the delivery list without a date then The returned file contains that order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user opens the dashboard, the portal shall return counts of orders in Received, Picking and Out for delivery status, non-Cancelled orders due for delivery today, and Unpaid and Overdue invoices.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 3 Received, 1 Picking and 2 Out for delivery orders, 2 non-Cancelled orders due today, 4 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice when A staff user requests the dashboard then The returned count fields for received, picking, outForDelivery, dueToday, unpaid and overdue are 3, 1, 2, 2, 4 and 1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user opens the dashboard, the portal shall return the count of orders in Confirmed status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 1 Confirmed order when A staff user requests the dashboard then The returned confirmed count field is 1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff user opens the dashboard, the portal shall return the count of failed stock imports since the last successful import.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 1 failed import after the last successful import when A staff user requests the dashboard then The returned failedImports count field is 1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the most recent stock import has failed, the portal shall show the latest import result, with failure time and reason, on the staff dashboard.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The latest import log record has status 'Failed' when A staff user requests the dashboard and the stock import list then The dashboard response field latestImportFailed is true and the returned import list shows the failed record with time and reason\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order's status becomes Delivered, the portal shall create one invoice for it with the next sequential prefixed invoice number, customer, the company's billing address, the order number, the invoice date, the order lines at order-time prices, the net total, the configured tax rate and tax amount, the gross total and payment status Unpaid.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Out for delivery order with net total 100.00, tax rate 20% and last invoice INV-000049 when Staff set it to Delivered then One invoice record exists with number INV-000050, net 100.00, tax rate 20%, tax 20.00, gross 120.00 and status Unpaid\",\n    \"Given A Picking order when The Buyer lists invoices then The returned list contains no invoice for that order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall report an unpaid invoice's payment status as Overdue once more than the configured number of days have passed since its invoice date, as Unpaid before that, and as Paid once payment is recorded.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Overdue days 30 and an unpaid invoice dated 1 March when The invoice-status calculator is called for 31 March and for 1 April then The returned values are Unpaid and Overdue\",\n    \"Given An invoice dated 1 January that is marked paid when The invoice-status calculator is called for 1 April then The returned value is Paid\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user lists invoices, the portal shall return invoice number, order number, invoice date, gross total and payment status for every invoice of the Buyer's own company, or of all companies for staff.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A has 2 invoices for orders placed by different Buyers, company B has 1 when Buyer A1 lists invoices then The returned list has 2 rows with invoiceNumber, orderNumber, invoiceDate, grossTotal and status fields\",\n    \"Given The same invoices when A staff user lists invoices then The returned list has 3 rows\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Unpaid invoices for Acme Garage and Fleet Co and a paid invoice for Acme Garage when Staff list invoices filtered by customer Acme Garage and status Unpaid then The returned list contains only the unpaid Acme Garage invoice\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer of the invoice's company or a staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF file containing the invoice number, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, lines with quantities and prices, net, tax and gross totals, payment status, and the distributor's logo and company details from settings.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Invoice INV-000050 for ORD-000124 with gross 120.00 when A Buyer of that company downloads it then The response status is 200, the content type is application/pdf and the text extracted from the file contains INV-000050, ORD-000124, the billing address and 120.00\",\n    \"Given The same invoice when An Office Staff user downloads it then The response status is 200 and the content type is application/pdf\",\n    \"Given The same invoice when A person opens the downloaded PDF then The logo and company details from settings are displayed in the header\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue